### Workstream A — Prepare your application documents

Start immediately

This is your first bottleneck. You should not wait until you have identified all 70 professors to prepare the documents.

### A1. CV

* Collect your existing CV, even if incomplete.

* Create a clean academic CV document.

* Add education: MSc, BSc, institutions, dates, grades and relevant coursework.

* Add your dissertation topic and a short description of the work.

* Add your research experience and mini-projects.

* Add computational and scientific skills.

* Add software and tools you can genuinely use.

* Add workshops, conferences, presentations and relevant academic activities.

* Add awards or academic distinctions, if applicable.

* Add referees only after confirming their willingness and contact details.

* Export as PDF.

* Check formatting, spelling, dates and consistency.

Important: do not wait for your project GitHub links to be ready.

Make the CV now. Include projects with an accurate description of their current status. Add GitHub links when the repositories are presentable. An unfinished project can still be described honestly as ongoing work, but do not present planned results as completed research.

### A2. Academic records and transcripts

Start immediately

